{"translation-revision-date":"2023-09-20 16:14+0000","generator":"WP-CLI\/2.12.0","source":"assets\/js\/admin\/api-docs\/api-docs.js","domain":"messages","locale_data":{"messages":{"":{"domain":"messages","lang":"es-ES","plural-forms":"nplurals=2; plural=(n != 1);"},"Required":["Requerido"],"Filters are the most comprehensive way to search for %s that match your criteria.":[""],"When using filters with <code class=\"get\">GET<\/code> it is best to JSON encode and then base64 encode the filters.":[""],"IDs of %s to include.":[""],"IDs of %s to exclude.":[""],"Search for %1$s using a search phrase. Will match %2$s.":[""],"The number of %s to return.":[""],"The number of %s per page.":[""],"The page of %s to return":[""],"The ID(s) of the %s to return.":[""],"Paginate through %s.":[""],"How to order %s.":[""],"Order %s by a specific column.":[""],"Whether to return the total number of %s matching the query.":[""],"An array of tag names or tag IDs. If passing names, if the tag does not exist it will be created. The array can be a mix of strings and IDs.":[""],"Any arbitrary key with any arbitrary value.":[""],"The meta object can contain any number of arbitrary key&rarr;value pairs.":[""],"Only return items created before this date.":[""],"Only return items created after this date.":[""],"Add another item":[""],"Are you sure you want to execute this API call? It will make real changes to the database.":[""],"Rest API":[""],"Endpoint":[""],"Identifiers":[""],"Parameters":[""],"Create a %s":[""],"Create an %s":[""],"Retrieve a %s":[""],"Retrieve an %s":[""],"Update a %s":[""],"Update an %s":[""],"Delete a %s":[""],"Delete an %s":[""],"List %s":[""],"Retrieve multiple %s using a query.":[""],"Create %s":[""],"Create multiple %s at once.":[""],"Update %s":[""],"Update multiple %s at once.":[""],"pluralized, deleting multiple items\u0004Delete %s":[""],"Delete multiple %s at once.":[""],"Retrieves a single %s.":[""],"Create a single %s.":[""],"Update a single %s.":[""],"Delete a single %s.":[""],"The data object contains all the necessary information for a new %s.":[""],"The ID of the %s to update.":[""],"Groundhogg offers a variety of authentication methods for you to use to access the REST API.":[""],"The Groundhogg REST API is permission based. Regardless of the authentication method, only users accessing the API with the required permissions will be able to perform requests.":[""],"Using API keys":[""],"Using API keys is an easy way to get started with the REST API. And is suitable for most backend applications.":[""],"When creating an API key, you are provided with a <b>token<\/b> and a <b>public key<\/b>. Both are required to authenticate requests.":[""],"You must add both to the header of your request.":[""],"Manage your API keys in the settings area.":[""],"Using application passwords":[""],"Using application passwords is the <b>BEST WAY<\/b> to use the Groundhogg REST API from external applications.":[""],"Applications passwords use basic authentication, which is supported by most external applications that you might want to integrate with Groundhogg.":[""],"For more on application passwords, see the <a href=\"https:\/\/make.wordpress.org\/core\/2020\/11\/05\/application-passwords-integration-guide\/\" target=\"_blank\">WordPress application password integration guide<\/a>.":[""],"Using a Nonce":[""],"If you are using the API from a front-end application, such as in the WordPress admin dashboard, you can use a <b>nonce<\/b> so that application passwords and API keys are not exposed.":[""],"For more on authenticating API requests using a nonce, see the <a href=\"https:\/\/developer.wordpress.org\/rest-api\/using-the-rest-api\/authentication\/\" target=\"_blank\">WordPress cookie authentication guide<\/a>.":[""]}}}